<title>UK: UK Treasury - PSBR to drop to 2.5% of GDP in 97/98.</title>
<headline>UK Treasury - PSBR to drop to 2.5% of GDP in 97/98.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK Treasury's financial statement and budget report (Red Book) said Britain's public sector borrowing requirement would fall to 2.5 percent of gross domestic product in 1997/98, from a projected 3.5 percent in 1996/97.</p>
<p>The Red Book said the 1997/98 PSBR would total 19 billion stg, compared with a forecast 26.5 billion in 1996/97.</p>
